The cell 'span differing from the document by a run of spaces / value differing from the span by case' specifies that the span is present in the document but differs only by a run of spaces, and the value differs from the span only in case. For the kernel `conformance.kernel.grounding`, the rule states it provides the grounding verdict with "no relaxation, value-in-span checked" [6ab8417a77f3b613]. Read as written, "no relaxation" implies that a span differing from the document by a run of spaces is not considered to occur in the document, which would lead to a verdict of SPAN_NOT_IN_DOCUMENT. In the rewritten text, I change the span to match the document character for character. The rule then implies a verdict of VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN, because the value still differs from the span by case and no relaxation is allowed for the value-in-span check. Thus, the verdict moves from SPAN_NOT_IN_DOCUMENT to VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN.